cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "paint.type — a cross-platform open-source image editor"
type: software
version: "0.2.0-rc.1"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
url: "https://github.com/metadatastician/paint-type"
repository-code: "https://github.com/metadatastician/paint-type"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
authors:
  - family-names: "Jewell"
    given-names: "Joshua"
    alias: "JoshuaJewell"
    email: "paint-type@pm.me"
abstract: >-
  paint.type is a cross-platform open-source image editor in the spirit of
  Paint.NET: capable enough for real work, simple enough to reach for without
  thinking. The image core (Ephapax) is Rust with linear types for tile safety
  over RGBA16F 64x64 tiles; the ABI is specified in Idris2 with dependent types
  proving pointer non-nullability, layout correctness and FFI safety; the FFI
  bridge is Zig with a C ABI; and the browser bridge layer is AffineScript
  compiled to typed-wasm. Tile merging for real-time collaboration is
  CRDT-compatible.
keywords:
  - "image-editor"
  - "cross-platform"
  - "formal-verification"
  - "idris2"
  - "zig"
  - "rust"
  - "crdt"
  - "rsr"
  - "paint-net"
license-files:
  - LICENSE
  - LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt
  - LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt
